course: dictionary
lesson: 11734
title: Awareness: knowing and noticing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Awareness is knowing about something or noticing it. When you have awareness of something, it is in your mind. «Sam had awareness of the bike coming up behind him, so he stepped onto the pavement.» Sam noticed the bike, so he was aware of it.
explain: Awareness can also mean understanding why something matters. «Our school ran a week to raise awareness of road safety.» The school wanted people to understand why road safety matters, not just to hear the words.
explain: To check a meaning, swap it into the sentence. Try «knowing» or «noticing» in place of awareness. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Words like raise, safety and week are clues.
fact: Awareness is a noun, and it is uncountable: we say some awareness, not an awareness.
fact: «Awareness» means knowing about something or noticing it.
fact: «Awareness» can also mean understanding why something matters.
fact: «Raise awareness» means help people learn about something.
fact: In nature, animals have awareness of predators, which means they notice danger nearby.
exercise: «The driver showed awareness of the children crossing the road.» What does awareness mean here? | Driving very fast past the children | Forgetting the children | *Noticing the children | Singing a song to the children
exercise: Our class held an awareness week about online safety. What was the week for? | To sell new computers | To stop all lessons for a day | To test how fast people can type | *To help people understand why online safety matters
exercise: «Mia has good self-awareness, so she knows her own strengths.» What does self-awareness mean? | Forgetting your own name | Being very tired after school | *Knowing and understanding yourself | Knowing the time of day
test: Ben kept awareness of strangers online and never shared his address. What does awareness mean here? | Forgetting something quickly | *Noticing and knowing about something | Liking something very much | Telling a secret loudly
test: Which phrase means help people learn about something? | a lack of awareness | *raise awareness | safety awareness is a shoe | awareness of the sea
exam: «Owls have awareness of movement in the grass.» What does this sentence suggest? | Owls cannot see at all | *Owls notice things moving nearby | Owls sleep all day in trees | Owls sing loudly at night
